English machine reading of the actual ARM A32 dqrls_ object
==========================================================

Source: ../dqrls.armv7-a32.disasm.txt
Status: first-pass textual operation concordance; NOT executable proof.
Address values are unlinked .text byte offsets, not runtime addresses.
Data .word literal pool entries are specifically marked non-instructions.
A32 instructions occupy 4 bytes; in normal sequential execution the
execution index moves from instruction address A to A+4. Branch, return,
PC writes, exceptions and unresolved linker relocations can change this.
Refer to the companion A32 machine-state document for PC+8 operand
reads, condition predicates, integer and FPSCR state, softfp ABI,
memory and external library boundaries.

